From f35018ed3363d1d3242c5909e2ce787b3fb226d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DrakeRamorayJr <179530612+DrakeRamorayJr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 02:13:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bare: close the bottom tab sheet without snapping and slide
 the button bar

Closing the bottom-bar tab sheet snapped in one frame: close() marked
the sheet closed before animating, so the morph parked on the bar and
the panel hid on the first frame while only the dim moved. The hand-off
back to the real bar also happened before the morph sat on the bar
rect, and the five-button bar, a compositor texture, stayed drawn under
the sheet and popped back at the end.

Back, tapping a tab and other programmatic closes now travel the sheet,
the morph pill and the page through the same progress path as a drag.
The close parks the morph on the measured bar rect with the toolbar
texture still suppressed, then swaps to the real bar on the next frame
and dismisses the window. Trailing bar icons are copied onto the morph
and fade with progress.

The five-button bar slides down and fades with the sheet progress and
is hidden from accessibility while the sheet is up. The compositor
layer follows through a new travel hook in BottomControlsCoordinator
and BottomControlsMediator, forwarded by ToolbarManager. The glass
window covers the vacated row. The navigation bar keeps its resting
colour while the sheet closes.

Top-bar sheet and side drawer are unchanged.
